Z||000001||RaeQwan||11-21-2000||01:22 AM||||*thinks back* I remember my first Fiero, well, I remember my brothers first fiero, a beautiful, and I do mean BEAUTIFUL silver 87 Coupe. I fell in love with it instantly. I remember myy dad talking about wanting a lil Fiero for as long as I can remember. When it came around two, an 87 & a 84 for 350$, I had to jump on it, well, my dad did. Bought em for me. We were fixing the 87 with misc parts from the 84(fasicas), but then I came across a white 88 coupe on my way from Myrtle Beach. I liked it, so me & my dad went and looked at it, the guy said it had a blown engine, but other than that it was good, missing a few interior parts but good. Only 200$ I fell in love with it, hadda have it. We went home... a hour or so later, maybe the next day, my parents left without telling me where they were going. a few hours later, here they come, the guy from the carlot pulling the car into my front yard. I freaked. I was like, My baby has come home. She's mine. that was last summer, near the end of the summer. me & my dad swapped the engine out of the 87 into the 88, and she's run beautiful since. She likes to eat up alt belts, but that will be fixed. As soon as I feel like muckin with the waterpump pulley. <P>"Its a thing called Fiero love"<P>Sorry for the longness, and thnx for listening. if you could follow my story.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/raeqwancfa.gif"> ||||reg||1
